<script type="module" src="@Assets["Components/Layout/ReconnectModal.razor.js"]"></script>

@* Blazor needs this element to exist. Its presence is what makes the framework use
   UserSpecifiedDisplay - class toggles plus a components-reconnect-state-changed event - instead of
   building its own reconnect UI, whose wording lands in the page source and from there in search
   results, making a perfectly healthy site look broken. It stays empty and hidden forever; the pill
   below is the only thing a user ever sees. *@
<dialog id="components-reconnect-modal" aria-hidden="true" data-nosnippet></dialog>

@* Deliberately wordless in the markup, for the same reason. Every string is written in by
   ReconnectModal.razor.js the first time a reconnect actually starts - which a crawler, fetching a
   page once against a healthy circuit, never triggers. What the crawler sees is these empty spans. *@
<div id="st-reconnect-pill" class="st-reconnect-pill" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-nosnippet>
    <span class="st-reconnect-spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="st-reconnect-text"></span>
</div>
